  "worked_solution": "First, we evaluate the inner integral by integrating with respect to $x,$ treating $y$ and $z$ as constants:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{z}{\\int }_{0}^{y+z}2xyz\\,dx\\,dy\\,dz & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{z}[{\\int }_{0}^{y+z}2xyz\\,dx]dy\\,dz \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{z}[{x}^{2}yz]_{x=0}^{x=y+z}\\,dy\\,dz \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{z}(y+z)^{2}yz\\,dy\\,dz\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we evaluate the inner integral by integrating with respect to $y,$ treating $z$ as a constant:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{z}(y+z)^{2}yz\\,dy\\,dz & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}[{\\int }_{0}^{z}{y}^{3}z+2{y}^{2}{z}^{2}+y{z}^{3}\\,dy]dz \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{[\\frac{1}{4}{y}^{4}z+\\frac{2}{3}{y}^{3}{z}^{2}+\\frac{1}{2}{y}^{2}{z}^{3}]}_{y=0}^{y=z}\\,dz \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}\\frac{1}{4}{z}^{5}+\\frac{2}{3}{z}^{5}+\\frac{1}{2}{z}^{5}\\,dz \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}\\frac{17}{12}{z}^{5}\\,dz\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we integrate with respect to $z:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{2}\\frac{17}{12}{z}^{5}\\,dz & ={[\\frac{17}{72}{z}^{6}]}_{0}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{17}{72}\\cdot 64 \\\\  & =\\frac{136}{9}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
